{"id":"u-032dd0f6-7c55-4ca5-b35e-b823e83dc746","src":"community","title":"hypertrophy goddess 1.0","author":"Homegymgains","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/GnIKFD-hypertrophy-goddess-10","desc":"Most programs fail for one simple reason: they demand maximum effort before establishing structural stability. They toss beginners straight into high-fatigue, zero-RIR failure training, leading to joint strain, secondary muscle dominant takeovers, and stalled growth.\nThis 10-week, 2-Block curriculum is engineered like a precision performance vehicle. It bridges foundational neural mapping directly into brutal, stretch-mediated mechanical tension—yielding optimal glute and total-body development safely and predictably.\nPhase Breakdown: The Roadmap to Maximum Adaptation\nPHASE 1: The Blueprint & Neural Calibration (Weeks 1–5)\nBuilding the Chassis & Mapping the System\n Neurological Alignment: High-stability movements (Smith machine variations, fixed-path presses, and targeted bracing primers) teach your Central Nervous System (CNS) to isolate the target muscle without balance acting as a bottleneck.\n The RPE 8 Safety Buffer: Working strictly with 2 Reps in Reserve allows your brain and connective tissue to master motor unit recruitment patterns, building tendon tolerance and execution confidence before heavy loading begins.\nPHASE 2: The High-Tension Ramp-Up (Weeks 6–9)\nTurning Up the Torque & Loading the Stretch\n Stretch-Mediated Mechanics: We upgrade your movement profiles to deeper ranges of motion—introducing deficit lunges, deep squats, and specific line-of-pull adjustments to load target fibers in their fully lengthened states where hypertrophy stimulus peaks.\n Closing the RIR Gap: Rep ranges drop and intensity climbs to RPE 9 (1 Rep in Reserve). With mechanics locked in, we demand higher force output to recruit high-threshold motor units and force immediate muscular adaptation.\nPHASE 3: The Peak Mechanical Failure Test (Week 10)\nUnleashing Total Force Output\n 0 RIR Execution: The ultimate test of your 9-week progression. Because your execution, bracing, and joint alignment are bulletproof, you take your primary glute and compound drivers to absolute mechanical failure (0 RIR) with zero risk of form breakdown.","level":["Beginner","Novice","Intermediate"],"goals":["Women's","Strength","Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":4,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-09-30T00:49:16.151Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Full body A","Full body B","Full body C","Optional Glute/core"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Dead Bug","sets":[{"r":10}],"note":"10reps total"},{"n":"Glute Bridge (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"r":10}]},{"n":"Glute Bridge (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Single Arm Iso Row","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Box squat (smith)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":2}]}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Smith Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Bridged Hip Abduction","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Pallof Press Hold (cable)","sets":[{"sec":30,"secHi":45,"rpe":8}],"note":"Do on both sides then rest for 1min then do the second set"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Dead Bug","sets":[{"r":10}],"note":"This is a Warm up before the session starts"},{"n":"Glute Bridge (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"r":10}]},{"n":"Single Leg Hip Thrust","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Reverse Lunge (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Seated Shoulder Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Lateral Banded Walk","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"45 Degree Hyper","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"x":2}]}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Dead Bug","sets":[{"r":10}],"note":"Warm up for the actual work sets"},{"n":"Glute Bridge (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"r":10}],"note":"G